# Each line is a finding that is a deliberate choice for this demo, with the reason.

# The service is a public HTTP endpoint with no domain, so there is no certificate to put on it.
AVD-AWS-0053
AVD-AWS-0054

# The tasks must reach the image registry and the dataset host, and they sit in the default VPC
# with no NAT gateway; only the load balancer can reach them.
AVD-AWS-0104

# Log group and queue encryption with a customer-managed key: a KMS key costs money and adds
# nothing for logs that hold queries over a public benchmark.
AVD-AWS-0017

# CloudWatch alarms cannot publish to a topic encrypted with the AWS-managed SNS key; a customer
# key would be needed, with the same cost argument.
AVD-AWS-0095

# A demo meant to be destroyed after a few hours.
AVD-AWS-0177
